    {
      "id": "claim_4174b6ead2a64bb299405dc6607b6c09",
      "statement": "The current default model tiers (gpt-5.6-luna default, gpt-5.6-terra validator) replaced an original gpt-4o-mini/gpt-4o pairing; the repository's committed measurement of this migration shows that using gpt-5.6-luna as the validator tier dropped core-set correctness from 0.75 to 0.55 (a weaker structurer discards good content it cannot cite), and that swapping the default tier alone raised per-query cost roughly 2-4x due to more aggressive decomposition rather than per-call pricing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/baseline-report.md#L43-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6fcf4de041da0a052f2475f86dadd4dce876b6e86fb32b8089b1a09a9c101639:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/writeup.md#L255-L255",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:86713b4b01d2f6a2af5ef16d80dc3be20647ac61e428ecd5b158e43836c1658f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_688d4a107dd24aa49e9d9d9d1786ff44",
      "statement": "Cost was brought back down to the original ~$0.028/query baseline only after the model-tier migration was combined with a separate, non-model change (capping decomposition fan-out and adding a synthesis branch); this combined result is the one committed net-cost measurement for the migration in this repository and should not be read as evidence that model tier swaps in general are cost-neutral or beneficial.",
      "evidence": [
