        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1c1393591d744231803381b2cf42e93e",
      "statement": "Decomposition and retrieval-gap-fill have explicit fan-out limits independent of model choice: decomposition always retrieves the parent query plus at most HC_RAG_MAX_SUBQUERIES additional branches, and retrieval evaluation permits only one gap-fill round (requiring gap_round == 0, retaining at most three additional queries, and marking the round used before routing to generation).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/services/models.py#L35-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9490639022b162a664b219a6b29920a0894860b78502f7bb5cbe19710a9a92d8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1c4971e7ac9248c388a3fc35679072bf",
      "statement": "The retrieval arm (HC_RAG_RETRIEVER: weaviate/pageindex/pinecone) only swaps the per-collection search callable while routing, merging, and all downstream graph stages stay shared; Weaviate and Pinecone clients connect lazily on first use, PageIndex reads cached tree/chunk JSON files and opens no retrieval client (missing files direct the operator to run make index-pageindex), and OPENAI_API_KEY / PINECONE_API_KEY are required only at the lazy boundary where they are first needed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/services/models.py#L43-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:271d2ffb55100ed1af55c5f8e4aa32c728d25e4a56b1552ce9d5a49e0d0a8a44:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3bbebed69d9548fca42e45cb3b637051",
      "statement": "When HC_RAG_RERANKER=pinecone, the search fetches HC_RAG_RERANK_CANDIDATES documents per collection and Pinecone Inference reranks down to HC_RAG_RERANK_TOP_K; a rerank failure or empty ranking falls back to the search's own order truncated to top_k, so a reranker malfunction degrades result composition without failing the turn.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/services/models.py#L50-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5b3d7b350be2abb03ca4faa4f1d09e40a4906351dbedd6d89737d492aab4753:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d9fc0754eae24398b125ee1d81c8df08",
      "statement": "HC_RAG_CHECKPOINT selects the engine-owned checkpointer at initialization: empty or any value not beginning \"sqlite:\" selects InMemorySaver, a \"sqlite:<path>\" value enters an AsyncSqliteSaver context and runs schema setup, and SQLite support requires the graph-sqlite extra or initialization raises RuntimeError with that instruction.",
